# Accidental bare-name build output of ./tests/sandboxes/mcp
/mcp

# Same for ./cmd/palai-agentd, and this one is worth naming: it is a 3.8 MB Mach-O, and the residue
# scans this tree runs use `grep`, which is ugrep here and SKIPS BINARIES — so a stray build of it
# sits in an evidence sweep's blind spot while the sweep reports clean.
/palai-agentd

# Karsilastirma ekran goruntuleri (referans vs bizimki). Uretilir, versiyonlanmaz.
.shots/

# API READBACK DUMPS AT THE ROOT, and this one is worth naming for what it nearly cost. A
# `details-readback.json` sat here from 2026-08-05 to 2026-08-06 — a raw Slack conversations.history
# response carrying team, app and bot ids and message text — untracked, UNIGNORED, at the top of a
# PUBLIC repository. Nothing was wrong with capturing it; what was wrong is where it landed, one
# `git add -A` away from being published. That command is already forbidden here because this checkout
# is shared, and a file like this is exactly the reason the rule exists rather than a general caution.
#
# Captures belong in the session scratchpad. This pattern is the net under that habit, not a substitute
# for it: it catches the shape (`*-readback.json`) and only at the root, so a fixture that legitimately
# carries the name inside a test corpus is unaffected.
/*-readback.json
